                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Playing as Barney makes the experience a little different from the original Half Life, mainly because you are following the events as a security guard simply trying to survive the chaos at black mesa, the campaign is quite short, but i thought the pacing was very good and I didn’t feel it was dragging on just to make it last longer, the atmosphere remains excellent and there are some really cool situations involving the scientists and other staff at the facility, the main issue is that it doesnt introduce as many new features as Opposing Force, the arsenal is more limited, and I missed having more new weapons or enemies, even so, I dont think this is a major drawback, because the campaign is fun and well put together, its not the best Half Life expansion, but I really enjoyed the experience, its simple, short and gets straight to the point, and I think its worth playing, especially if you enjoyed the first Half Life.",
